      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to calculate the magnitude of their cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\).\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is given by the determinant of the following matrix:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product can be computed as follows:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying each component:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nTo verify the result, we can use Python code to compute the cross product and its magnitude.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors\nu = np.array([3, 1, -2])\nv = np.array([1, -3, 4])\n\n# Compute the cross product\ncross_product = np.cross(u, v)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\nprint((cross_product, magnitude))\n```",
