      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we will calculate the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors.\n\n1. Compute the cross product of \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\):\n\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n   This determinant expands as follows:\n\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} (1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)) - \\mathbf{j} (3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1) + \\mathbf{k} (3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1)\n   \\]\n\n   Simplify the terms within the parentheses:\n\n   \\[\n   = \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   = \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the cross product is:\n\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the magnitude of the cross product vector:\n\n   \\[\n   \\left\\| \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} \\right\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2}\n   \\]\n\n   Compute the squares:\n\n   \\[\n   = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   = \\sqrt{300}\n   \\]\n\n   Simplify further:\n\n   \\[\n   = \\sqrt{100 \\times 3}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   = 10 \\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10 \\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
