      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to compute the magnitude of their cross product. The area of the parallelogram formed by two vectors in \\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\) is given by the magnitude of their cross product.\n\nFirst, we compute the cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nExpanding the determinant, we get:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\\):\n\\[\n\\left\\| \\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} \\right\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{290}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{290}}\n\\]",
